No uv.lock exists for branch PY-069, and none can -- but NOT for the
reason the 3.6 and 3.7 families gave.

uv itself works perfectly on Python 3.8.18. poetry-core 1.9.1 works too.
They cannot work TOGETHER:

    $ uv lock
    error: No `project` table found in: `pyproject.toml`

    $ uv sync
    error: No `project` table found in: `pyproject.toml`

uv requires PEP 621. poetry-core 1.9.1 predates poetry-core 2 and
writes [tool.poetry] instead. Neither half is broken and neither
is at fault; the metadata shapes are simply incompatible.

This is the only failure of its kind in the corpus, and it is a
different CLASS from the earlier families' uv failures, which
were interpreter floors. dataset.json records it as
nonFunctionalClass: "metadata-shape incompatibility".
